  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "The current best is config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.639). The image modality alone is weak (ResNet50: 0.208), yet it still adds ~5% over RNA-only in the multimodal setting, suggesting the image features contribute useful complementary signal. The most natural single-variable extension is to upgrade the image encoder from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L while keeping everything else identical (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion). This isolates the effect of image representation quality. If ViT-L provides richer spatial/texture features, it should push accuracy above 0.639; if not, it confirms the bottleneck is elsewhere. With only 2 experiments remaining, this is the highest-value exploitation of the current best direction, and it avoids the transformer aggregation which was clearly inferior to avgpool in all RNA-only comparisons (0.519 vs 0.591)."
}

